  "notes": "creep: American lobster, about half a metre with the claws: dark mottled olive-brown above, orange-tinged beneath, the claws and legs tipped red-orange, long red antennae. Lives on the rocky bay floor, lies up against a rock and walks slowly from one high spot to the next; pressed, it shoots off backwards with a flip of its tail. The creep mover pales it toward the sand as you come close, which a lobster would not do. v2: carapace, abdomen and tail fan are a few large overlapping ellipsoids; the abdomen and fan are their own `tail` bone so the body fits a 32^3 window; claws and legs are segments and flattened ellipsoids; eyes are small ellipsoids.",
